---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import AgentPrompt from '../components/home/AgentPrompt.astro';
import DotField from '../components/home/DotField.astro';
import SharedState from '../components/home/SharedState.astro';
import CounterExample from '../components/home/CounterExample.astro';
import ProjectFooter from '../components/ProjectFooter.astro';

const steps = [
  ['01', 'Create', 'Start a project with the CLI.', '/cli/create-project/'],
  ['02', 'Write', 'Define contract logic in Rust.', '/contracts/'],
  ['03', 'Test', 'Check native and RV32 execution.', '/cli/build-and-test/'],
  ['04', 'Deploy', 'Fund and initialize on Devnet.', '/cli/deploy-and-call/'],
  ['05', 'Connect', 'Call with typed bindings.', '/typescript/'],
];
---
<StarlightPage hasSidebar={true} frontmatter={{
  title: 'Stellar Thruput',
  description: 'Stellar Thruput is a moonshot project exploring abundant compute through parallel execution over shared state.',
  template: 'splash', pagefind: false, prev: false, next: false,
}}>
  <div class="home-page not-content">
    <noscript><nav class="home-fallback" aria-label="Site navigation"><a href="/get-started/">Documentation</a><a href="/start/build-with-an-agent/">Build with an agent</a></nav></noscript>
    <section id="hero" aria-labelledby="_top">
      <DotField />
      <div class="home-container hero-content">
        <h1 id="_top">The blockchain built <br /><span class="hero-final-line">for <span class="abundance">abundance<span class="hero-cursor" aria-hidden="true">_</span></span></span></h1>
        <p class="hero-description">Smart contracts that share state. Parallel execution.<br />No conventional gas fees.</p>
        <AgentPrompt />
        <nav class="hero-links" aria-label="Start exploring"><a href="/get-started/contract/">Follow the guided quickstart <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/architecture/">Understand Stellar Thruput <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="shared-state">
      <div class="home-container split">
        <div class="section-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">01 / A different starting point</p>
          <h2 id="shared-state">Shared state.<br />Compatible changes.</h2>
          <p>Stellar Thruput is a moonshot project built around a simple thesis: compute doesn't have to be scarce if transactions don't have to execute sequentially.</p>
          <p>A shared counter is a small example. Three transactions read the same snapshot and record compatible increments. Their changes combine without one transaction waiting to read another's result. Balances and collections have their own rules.</p>
          <p>No decisions have been made about mainnet or Stellar Thruput's relationship to Stellar.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works/execution-model/">Explore the execution model <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <SharedState />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section differences" aria-labelledby="differences">
      <div class="home-container differences-layout">
        <div class="section-copy"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Why Stellar Thruput</p><h2 id="differences">More room for application logic.</h2><p>Match orders, resolve a game turn, or run an auction alongside the assets it moves. Parallel execution aims to make compute abundant by removing the sequential execution bottleneck.</p></div>
        <div class="difference-list">
          <article id="concurrency"><span class="number">01</span><div><h3>Parallel execution, shared state</h3><p>Storage types let compatible changes combine across transactions. Your choice of storage defines the merge rules.</p><a class="text-link" href="/programming-model/storage-types/">Choose your storage <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
          <article id="compute"><span class="number">02</span><div><h3>No conventional gas fees</h3><p>Gas meters computation without a token fee. Native tokens are still required for storage and scheduling capacity under load.</p><a class="text-link" href="/programming-model/execution/#gas">Understand gas limits <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
          <article id="capacity"><span class="number">03</span><div><h3>Balance-based capacity</h3><p>Unlocked native-token balances provide scheduling capacity. A root transaction's declared gas limit determines how much capacity it uses. The experimental network's token has no monetary value.</p><a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works/storage-economics/#balance-proportional-scheduling">Explore scheduling <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
          <article id="storage"><span class="number">04</span><div><h3>Refundable storage deposits</h3><p>Stored data locks native tokens as a deposit. Delete the data to reclaim that deposit.</p><a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works/storage-economics/#storage-refundable-deposits">Understand storage deposits <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section developer-section" aria-labelledby="developer-experience">
      <div class="home-container">
        <div class="split">
          <div class="section-copy"><p class="eyebrow">03 / From contract to application</p><h2 id="developer-experience">Write Rust. Build something you can use.</h2><p>Create, test, deploy, and inspect contracts with a complete CLI. Generate TypeScript bindings to call them from your application. Give your coding agent the <code>groundhog</code> skill and local docs to work from the same tools and instructions.</p><a class="text-link" href="/tutorials/build-a-counter/">Build a counter, step by step <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
          <CounterExample />
        </div>
        <ol class="workflow" role="list">{steps.map(([number, title, description, href]) => <li><a href={href}><span class="number">{number}</span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></div></a></li>)}</ol>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="home-container"><ProjectFooter /></div>
  </div>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
  .home-page { isolation: isolate; color-scheme: only dark; background: var(--brand-background); color: var(--brand-foreground); font-family: var(--sl-font); }
  .home-container { width: calc(100% - 2.5rem); max-width: 77.5rem; margin-inline: auto; }
  .home-fallback, .hero-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem 2rem; }
  .home-fallback { justify-content: center; padding: 1rem; }
  .home-page a { color: var(--sl-color-text-accent); }
  .home-page a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .25em; }
  #hero { position: relative; overflow: hidden; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--brand-border); }
  .hero-content { position: relative; padding-block: 5rem 3.5rem; text-align: center; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0; font: 400 .75rem/1.5 var(--sl-font-mono); letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--brand-muted); }
  .home-page h1 { margin: 1.5rem 0; font-size: clamp(2.0625rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.06em; text-wrap: balance; }
  .hero-final-line { white-space: nowrap; }
  .abundance { color: var(--brand-accent); }
  .hero-description { max-width: 56ch; margin: 0 auto; font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.6; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .hero-cursor { display: inline-block; width: 0; animation: cursor-blink 1.4s steps(1) infinite; }
  @keyframes cursor-blink { 50% { opacity: 0; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .hero-cursor { animation: none; } }
  .hero-links { justify-content: center; margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  .hero-links a, .text-link { text-decoration: none; }
  .home-section { padding-block: 3.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--brand-border); }
  .home-section.developer-section { padding-block: 3.5rem; }
  .split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2.5rem; align-items: center; }
  .section-copy { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: start; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .home-page h2 { margin: 0; max-width: 24ch; font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -.04em; text-wrap: balance; }
  .section-copy p:not(.eyebrow) { margin: 0; max-width: 56ch; color: var(--brand-muted); font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .home-page h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .differences { background: #141511; }
  .differences-layout { display: grid; gap: 2.5rem; align-items: start; }
  .difference-list { display: grid; gap: 2.5rem; }
  .difference-list article { display: flex; gap: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--brand-border); padding-top: 1.5rem; }
  .difference-list article:first-child { border-top: 0; padding-top: 0; }
  .number { color: var(--brand-accent); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono); }
  .difference-list p { color: var(--brand-muted); line-height: 1.65; }
  .difference-list p { max-width: 56ch; }
  .workflow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; list-style: none; padding: 1.5rem 0 0; margin: 2rem 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--brand-border); }
  .workflow li { min-width: 0; }
  .workflow a { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: .75rem; height: 100%; color: var(--brand-foreground); text-decoration: none; }
  .workflow a > div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .375rem; }
  .workflow .number { flex-shrink: 0; }
  .home-page .workflow a:hover { color: var(--brand-accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .workflow p { margin: 0; color: var(--brand-muted); }
  @media (min-width: 701px) {
    .home-container { width: calc(100% - 4rem); }
    .hero-content { padding-block: 6rem 4rem; }
    .home-section { padding-block: 5rem; }
    .split { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .difference-list { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .difference-list article:nth-child(2) { border-top: 0; padding-top: 0; }
    .workflow { grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; }
    .workflow a { font-size: .9375rem; }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1101px) { .home-container { width: calc(100% - 6rem); } .differences-layout { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 2fr); } }
  @media (min-width: 1700px) { .home-container { max-width: 88.75rem; } .hero-content { padding-block: 4rem 5rem; } .home-page h1 { font-size: 5rem; } }
</style>
